---
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Pricing" description="LiteMCP Composer is complete Apache-2.0 software. The managed-cloud preview is currently free under published quotas; future hosted plans will price operated capacity and support.">
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Pricing"
    title="Open product. Optional operated service."
    description="Evaluate and run the complete Apache-2.0 product today. The managed-cloud preview is currently free under published quotas; future hosted plans will cover operated capacity, reliability, and support once their terms are published."
    signal="Pre-1.0 product and service model"
  />

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="shell price-grid">
      <article class="price-card">
        <span class="price-card__label">Managed cloud · Preview</span>
        <h2>Community-cloud preview</h2>
        <div class="price-card__price">Free</div>
        <p>The public preview is live with registration controlled and no availability or support commitment.</p>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>5 servers and 5 compositions per organization</li>
          <li>25 active sessions</li>
          <li>1,000 tool calls per UTC day</li>
          <li>Configuration export in preview</li>
          <li>No uptime, capacity, or support commitment</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="button" href="/cloud">Managed cloud details</a>
      </article>
      <article class="price-card price-card--featured">
        <span class="price-card__label">Your infrastructure · Preview</span>
        <h2>Self-hosted source</h2>
        <div class="price-card__price">Free</div>
        <p>The complete product core and deployment assets under Apache License 2.0.</p>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Docker images and Compose configuration</li>
          <li>Helm chart lint/render validation</li>
          <li>Policy and audit vertical slice</li>
          <li>Identity federation wiring in preview</li>
          <li>No call-home requirement</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="button button--primary" href="/docs/self-hosting">Deployment guide</a>
      </article>
      <article class="price-card">
        <span class="price-card__label">Professional services · Planned</span>
        <h2>On-prem support</h2>
        <div class="price-card__price">Not published</div>
        <p>Future engagements may be scoped for topology, environments, responsibilities, and response needs.</p>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Architecture and installation</li>
          <li>Identity and vault integration</li>
          <li>HA, backup, and upgrades</li>
          <li>Future security and support terms</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="button" href="/enterprise">Service scope</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section content-section--subtle">
    <div class="shell split-layout">
      <div class="split-layout__aside">
        <p class="eyebrow">Plain-language model</p>
        <h2>Hosted plans pay for an operated service, not permission to self-host.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="principle-list">
        <li><span>01</span><div><strong>Managed cloud is currently a free preview</strong><p>Preview quotas are published and enforced. Future paid plans, capacity commitments, and SLAs will apply only after separate service terms are published.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>02</span><div><strong>Self-hosting is independently operable</strong><p>The public distribution has no hosted entitlement check, mandatory call-home path, or commercial quota by default; operators may set local governance limits.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>03</span><div><strong>Services buy operations and responsibility</strong><p>Future contracts can cover managed capacity, human work, release support, escalation, and response—not access to a secret product binary.</p></div></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
